.TH JOBWRAP 1 "October 2026" "jobwrap 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jobwrap \- wrap a locally launched Linux process with monitoring and control
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jobwrap
run [\fIOPTIONS\fR] -- \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENTS\fR...]
.br
.B jobwrap \fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBjobwrap\fR runs \fICOMMAND\fR inside a pseudo-terminal so it behaves exactly
like a normal foreground command, while a per-user daemon provides a web
interface, an HTTP API, and scoped control of the process.
.PP
Start jobs explicitly with \fBjobwrap run [OPTIONS] -- COMMAND [ARGS...]\fR.
Unknown subcommands, bare executable names, and the old \fBwrap\fR form are
rejected before a process is started. \fBstatus JOB_ID\fR is an alias for
\fBshow JOB_ID\fR, never an executable launch.
.SH WRAPPER OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-name \fINAME\fR
A human-readable name for the job.
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fINAME\fR
The access profile to use (defaults to the configured profile).
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-detach
Start the wrapper in a separate systemd user service, outside the launching
terminal or agent's process tree and cgroup. Requires systemd-run and a working
user manager. Returns zero after job registration, before workload completion.
Check the job state and application readiness separately. Preserves the caller's
working directory, arguments, and environment. Conflicts with --no-web.
.TP
.B \-\-no-web
Do not start or use the web server.
.TP
.B \-\-no-record
Do not record terminal output to the log.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B run [\fIOPTIONS\fR] -- \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
Run a foreground job, or an independent user service with --detach (-d).
.TP
.B list
List registered jobs.
.TP
.B show \fIJOB\fR
Show detailed information about one job.
.TP
.B status \fIJOB\fR
Alias for show. Includes the final exit code or termination signal.
.TP
.B logs \fIJOB\fR [\-\-offset N]
Print a job's recorded output.
.TP
.B signal \fIJOB\fR \fISIGNAL\fR
Send a named signal (int, term, stop, cont, kill) to a job's process group.
.TP
.B stop \fIJOB\fR
Send SIGTERM to a job's process group.
.TP
.B open [\fIJOB\fR]
Open the web interface in a browser.
.TP
.B daemon status|start|stop|restart
Manage the per-user daemon. Use \fBdaemon start \-\-foreground\fR to run
attached to the terminal.
.TP
.B config path|init|validate|effective|explain
Manage the configuration.
.TP
.B auth set-password|remove-password|status
Manage the browser password.
.TP
.B token create|list|revoke
Manage scoped API tokens.
.TP
.B attach \fIJOB\fR
Reserved for experimental interactive attachment; currently returns an error.
.TP
.B launch \fIEXECUTABLE\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
Experimental daemon-side launch. Disabled by default; requires explicit
configuration. See \fBjobwrap launch \-\-help\fR for options.
.TP
.B attach-launch \fILAUNCH_ID\fR
Internal one-time launch helper used by the daemon's terminal backends.
.TP
.B inspect \fITARGET\fR
Inspect static executable metadata and man pages.
.TP
.B terminals
List registered terminals.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Foreground run returns the child's exit code. Signals are reported as 128 plus
the signal number. Detached run returns zero once registration is confirmed;
the child result is reported by show/status. Parsing errors exit 2 without
starting a job; internal failures return nonzero. A detached startup timeout
may have an uncertain outcome: inspect the reported job ID and service before
retrying.
.SH DETACHED LIFETIME
Each detached job belongs to jobwrap-job-JOB_ID.service. Use jobwrap stop JOB_ID
and confirm its final state. If daemon monitoring is lost, inspect the service
with systemctl --user status and journalctl --user -u, or terminate it with
systemctl --user stop using that exact service name.
.PP
Services survive daemon shutdown but wrapper reconnection is not implemented:
a restarted daemon marks their records disconnected and cannot record/control
them. User-manager shutdown, logout policy, reboot, and explicit service stops
can still terminate jobs. No boot persistence or automatic restart is configured.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/jobwrap/config.toml
Configuration (see \fBjobwrap.toml(5)\fR).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/jobwrap/daemon.sock
The private daemon socket.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/jobwrap/jobwrap.db
SQLite database.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/jobwrap/logs/
Append-only terminal logs.
.SH SECURITY
See \fI/usr/share/doc/jobwrap/README.md.gz\fR and the security model. The daemon
binds to loopback by default. HTTP API process creation is disabled by default;
local detached launches use the private owner-authenticated Unix socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jobwrapd (8),
.BR jobwrap.toml (5)
